# /skin-designer — Per-game canvas skin implementation

This rule triggers the **skin-designer** skill. Read `.claude/skills/skin-designer/SKILL.md` and follow it strictly.

## What this does

- Takes a **game slug** (e.g. `asteroids`, `tetris`) — **one game per session**
- Implements three skins: **classic** (default), **retro**, **neon** — all readable on dark CRT canvas
- Creates shared skin infra (`types`, `player-skin`, selector) **only if missing**
- Updates inventory in `references/skin-designer/game-with-themes.md`

## What this does NOT do

- Apply skins to all playables in one go
- Mark specs as `Aprobado`
- Skin placeholders until integrated (unless explicitly requested)

## Supporting files

- `.claude/skills/skin-designer/SKILL.md` — five-phase workflow and hard rules
- `.claude/skills/skin-designer/palette-guide.md` — classic / retro / neon definitions
- `.claude/skills/skin-designer/dark-mode-checklist.md` — contrast and verification
- `references/skin-designer/game-with-themes.md` — skin coverage inventory (read at start, update at end)

## Workflow summary

1. **Context** — read `game-with-themes.md`, target engine, palette guide
2. **Confirm game** — single slug from argument or user prompt
3. **Tokens** — `lib/games/{slug}/skins.ts`; classic = current colors
4. **Implement** — engine + React wiring + shared UI if needed
5. **Persist** — update game row + append session in `game-with-themes.md`, then **STOP**

## Subagent

For a clean context, delegate to [`.cursor/agents/skin-designer.md`](.cursor/agents/skin-designer.md) when the user explicitly asks for the `@skin-designer` subagent.

## Example invocations

```
@skin-designer snake
@skin-designer audit
```
